IMPORT prelude

-- Transboundary Haze Pollution Act 2014 (Singapore) -- when there is "haze pollution in Singapore" (s 2), who participates in
-- the management of another entity (s 3), the offences and civil duty for causing or condoning haze pollution (ss 5, 6), the
-- defences (s 7), the evidential presumptions (s 8), when a preventive measures notice may be given (s 9), the information,
-- obstruction and officer offences (ss 10(6), 10(7), 14, 16), service by registered post (s 15(2)(b)) and composition (s 19).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/THPA2014.txt. The deposit says the revised
-- edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the
-- only later amendment annotated in the body is "[Act 31 of 2022 wef 01/11/2022]" on s 17 (notice to attend court).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0080 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to the liability provisions and the offences and penalties a business or its officers meet. Not encoded:
-- the investigation powers themselves (ss 10(1) to (5), (8) to (11), 11), public-servant status and immunity (ss 12, 13), the
-- other modes of service (s 15(1), (2)(a)), notice to attend court, jurisdiction, notices, inaccuracies, evidence, forms and
-- regulations (ss 17, 18, 20 to 24). The prescribed air quality index number (s 2(2)(a)) and the prescribed compoundable offences
-- (s 19(1)) are in regulations that were not retrieved, so the index number is a parameter and composition is computed as a
-- ceiling only.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Transboundary Haze Pollution Act 2014 -- liability`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `2 -- haze pollution in Singapore`

-- s 2(2): a poor air quality episode occurs when "(a) the air quality index for any part of Singapore reaches the prescribed number
-- on the index or higher; and (b) for the next 24 hours or longer, the air quality index for the same part or any other part of
-- Singapore remains at or reaches that number so prescribed or higher." The prescribed number is not in the Act.
GIVEN `the highest reading` IS A NUMBER, `the prescribed index number` IS A NUMBER, `hours at or above it afterwards` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a poor air quality episode occurs` IF
        `the highest reading` AT LEAST `the prescribed index number`
    AND `hours at or above it afterwards` AT LEAST 24

-- s 2(1): "haze pollution in Singapore" means pollution of the environment in Singapore "comprising any poor air quality episode
-- involving smoke from any land or forest fire wholly outside Singapore"; "land or forest fire" includes coal seam fire, peat fire
-- or plantation fire.
GIVEN `there is a poor air quality episode` IS A BOOLEAN, `it involves smoke from a land or forest fire` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the fire is wholly outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is haze pollution in Singapore` IF
        `there is a poor air quality episode`
    AND `it involves smoke from a land or forest fire`
    AND `the fire is wholly outside Singapore`

-- s 2(1): "entity" means "any sole proprietorship, partnership, corporation or other body of persons, whether corporate or
-- unincorporate". Sections 5 and 6 are framed only against an entity.
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a sole proprietorship`
    `a partnership`
    `a company`
    `an unincorporated association`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an entity` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3 -- participation in the management of another entity`

-- s 3: the first entity participates "if, and only if" (a) it "actually participates in the management or operational affairs";
-- (b) it "exercises decision-making control over any business decision" by the second entity to engage in (or condone) haze-causing
-- conduct on the second entity's land outside Singapore; or (c) it exercises manager-level control and assumes responsibility for
-- (i) the overall day-to-day management of such decisions or (ii) "all or a substantial part of the operational functions (as
-- distinguished from financial or administrative functions)".
GIVEN `actually participates in management or operations` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `controls the decision to engage in haze-causing conduct on the land` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `manages day-to-day decisions on such conduct` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is responsible for a substantial part of the operational functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `participates in the management of the second entity` IF
        `actually participates in management or operations`
    OR  `controls the decision to engage in haze-causing conduct on the land`
    OR  `manages day-to-day decisions on such conduct`
    OR  `is responsible for a substantial part of the operational functions`

§§ `7 -- defences`

-- s 7(1): a defence to ss 5(1), 5(3), 6(1), 6(2) if the accused or defendant proves, on a balance of probabilities, that the haze
-- "was caused solely by (a) a grave natural disaster or phenomenon; or (b) an act of war". It is a whole defence, so it is an input
-- to each liability rule below.
--
-- s 7(2): to the CAUSING limb of s 5(1) / 6(1): the conduct "was by another person acting without the accused's or defendant's
-- knowledge or consent, or contrary to the accused's or defendant's wishes or instructions; but that other person cannot be --
-- (a) any employee or agent ...; (b) any person engaged, directly or indirectly, ... to carry out any work on the land ... and any
-- of that person's employees; or (c) any person who has a customary right ... and with whom the accused ... has an agreement or
-- arrangement" relating to farming or forestry operations on that land. s 7(4) is the same for s 5(3) / 6(2), extended to the
-- second entity's employees, agents, contractors and customary-right partners.
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    `nobody else`
    `a stranger trespassing on the land`
    `an employee`
    `an agent`
    `a contractor engaged to work on the land`
    `a contractor's employee`
    `a customary-right holder with a farming agreement`
    `a customary-right holder with no agreement`

GIVEN `the other person` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the other person can found the defence` IF
    CONSIDER `the other person`
    WHEN `a stranger trespassing on the land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a customary-right holder with no agreement` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 7(3): to the CONDONING limb: "(a) the accused or defendant took all such measures as are (or were at the material time)
-- reasonable to prevent such conduct by the other entity or individual; and (b) if the conduct ... already occurred, ... took all
-- such measures as are ... reasonable to stop that conduct from continuing or to substantially reduce the detriment".
DECLARE Limb IS ONE OF
    `causing or contributing`
    `condoning another's conduct`

GIVEN `the limb` IS A Limb, `the other person` IS AN Actor, `acted without knowledge or consent or against instructions` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took reasonable measures to prevent` IS A BOOLEAN, `the other's conduct had already occurred` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took reasonable measures to stop or reduce it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the limb defence is made out` IF
    CONSIDER `the limb`
    WHEN `causing or contributing` THEN
            `the other person can found the defence` `the other person`
        AND `acted without knowledge or consent or against instructions`
    WHEN `condoning another's conduct` THEN
            `took reasonable measures to prevent`
        AND ((NOT `the other's conduct had already occurred`) OR `took reasonable measures to stop or reduce it`)

§§ `5 -- offences`

-- s 5(1): "An entity shall be guilty of an offence if -- (a) the entity -- (i) engages in conduct (whether in or outside Singapore)
-- which causes or contributes to any haze pollution in Singapore; or (ii) engages in conduct ... that condones any conduct ... by
-- another entity or individual which causes or contributes ...; and (b) there is haze pollution in Singapore at or about the time
-- of that conduct by that entity."
GIVEN `the accused` IS A Person, `engaged in or condoned haze-causing conduct` IS A BOOLEAN, `haze pollution at or about the time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `caused solely by disaster or war` IS A BOOLEAN, `a limb defence is made out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `guilty under section 5(1)` IF
        `is an entity` `the accused`
    AND `engaged in or condoned haze-causing conduct`
    AND `haze pollution at or about the time`
    AND (NOT `caused solely by disaster or war`)
    AND (NOT `a limb defence is made out`)

-- s 5(3): an entity is guilty if "(a) the entity participates in the management of another entity ...; (b) the second entity is an
-- owner or occupier of any land situated outside Singapore; (c) the second entity" engages in or condones haze-causing conduct; and
-- "(d) there is haze pollution in Singapore at or about the time". The s 7(4) defence is passed in as a boolean.
GIVEN `the accused` IS A Person, `participates in the second entity's management` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the second entity owns or occupies land outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the second entity engaged in or condoned haze-causing conduct` IS A BOOLEAN, `haze pollution at or about the time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `caused solely by disaster or war` IS A BOOLEAN, `the section 7(4) defence is made out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `guilty under section 5(3)` IF
        `is an entity` `the accused`
    AND `participates in the second entity's management`
    AND `the second entity owns or occupies land outside Singapore`
    AND `the second entity engaged in or condoned haze-causing conduct`
    AND `haze pollution at or about the time`
    AND (NOT `caused solely by disaster or war`)
    AND (NOT `the section 7(4) defence is made out`)

-- s 5(2), (4): "(a) a fine not exceeding $100,000 for every day or part of a day that there is haze pollution in Singapore ...;
-- and (b) if it is proved that ... the entity had failed to comply with any preventive measures notice ..., then in addition ...,
-- a fine not exceeding $50,000 for every day or part of a day that the entity fails to comply". s 5(5): "the court must not impose
-- an aggregate fine exceeding $2 million." Days are counted with a part of a day as a whole day; there is no imprisonment.
GIVEN `days of haze` IS A NUMBER, `days of non-compliance with a preventive measures notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 5` MEANS
    `the lesser of`
        (`days of haze` TIMES 100000 PLUS `days of non-compliance with a preventive measures notice` TIMES 50000)
        2000000

§§ `6 -- civil liability`

-- s 6(1), (2): duties of "an entity" mirroring s 5(1) and (3). s 6(3): breach is "actionable conduct at the suit of any person in
-- Singapore who, in consequence of that breach -- (a) sustains any personal injury, contracts any disease or sustains any mental or
-- physical incapacity in Singapore, or dies in Singapore from that personal injury, disease or incapacity; (b) sustains any
-- physical damage to property in Singapore; or (c) sustains any economic loss, including a loss of profits, in Singapore."
-- s 6(4): actionable in Singapore "whether or not that conduct is also actionable in the foreign jurisdiction where that conduct
-- occurred". (That property abroad, and annoyance with no injury, incapacity, damage or loss, fall outside is an inference from the
-- closed list.)
DECLARE Harm IS ONE OF
    `personal injury in Singapore`
    `a disease contracted in Singapore`
    `mental incapacity in Singapore`
    `death in Singapore from haze-related illness`
    `physical damage to property in Singapore`
    `economic loss in Singapore`
    `lost profits in Singapore`
    `damage to property outside Singapore`
    `annoyance with no injury, damage or loss`

GIVEN `the harm` IS A Harm
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the harm is of an actionable kind` IF
    CONSIDER `the harm`
    WHEN `damage to property outside Singapore` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `annoyance with no injury, damage or loss` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the defendant` IS A Person, `the harm` IS A Harm, `the claimant is a person in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the defendant breached a section 6 duty` IS A BOOLEAN, `a section 7 defence is proved` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the conduct is actionable where it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant has a cause of action under section 6` IF
        `is an entity` `the defendant`
    AND `the harm is of an actionable kind` `the harm`
    AND `the claimant is a person in Singapore`
    AND `the defendant breached a section 6 duty`
    AND (NOT `a section 7 defence is proved`)
    AND (`the conduct is actionable where it occurred` OR TRUE)

§§ `8 -- presumptions`

-- s 8(1): where it is proved that there is haze pollution, a land or forest fire outside Singapore at or about the time, and "based
-- on satellite information, wind velocity and direction and other meteorological information ..., the smoke resulting from that
-- fire is moving in the direction of Singapore", it is presumed, until the contrary is proved, that the haze involves smoke from
-- that fire, "even though there may be, at or about the same time, any land or forest fire or other fire on any other land".
GIVEN `haze pollution is proved` IS A BOOLEAN, `a fire on land outside Singapore at about the time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `meteorological data shows the smoke moving toward Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `there are other fires at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the haze is presumed to involve smoke from that fire` IF
        `haze pollution is proved`
    AND `a fire on land outside Singapore at about the time`
    AND `meteorological data shows the smoke moving toward Singapore`
    AND (`there are other fires at the same time` OR TRUE)
    AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`)

-- s 8(4): an entity is presumed to own or occupy land if any of these maps show it so: (a) a map provided pursuant to a s 10
-- notice; (b) a map from a foreign government; (c) from a department or instrumentality of a foreign government; (d) "any map
-- provided by any prescribed person through any prescribed means".
DECLARE Map IS ONE OF
    `a map provided under a section 10 notice`
    `a foreign government map`
    `a foreign government agency map`
    `a map from a prescribed person by prescribed means`
    `a map published by a campaign group`
    `a map from a news report`

GIVEN `the map` IS A Map
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the map raises the ownership presumption` IF
    CONSIDER `the map`
    WHEN `a map published by a campaign group` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a map from a news report` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 8(2): where ownership or occupation is proved or presumed under (4), and the haze is proved or presumed under (1) to involve
-- smoke from a fire on that land, the owner or occupier is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have caused or condoned it.
GIVEN `ownership is proved or presumed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the haze is proved or presumed to involve smoke from the land` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner or occupier is presumed to have caused or condoned the haze` IF
        `ownership is proved or presumed`
    AND `the haze is proved or presumed to involve smoke from the land`
    AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`)

-- s 8(3): where "it is proved" that the first entity participates in the management of the second, and it is proved or presumed
-- under (2) that the second entity caused or condoned the haze, the first entity is presumed to have done so too. Participation
-- itself must be PROVED; it is not presumed.
GIVEN `participation is proved` IS A BOOLEAN, `the second entity's conduct is proved or presumed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the managing entity is presumed to have caused or condoned the haze` IF
        `participation is proved`
    AND `the second entity's conduct is proved or presumed`
    AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`)

§§ `9 -- preventive measures notice`

-- s 9(1): where "(a) there is air pollution of the environment in Singapore, or there is air pollution of the environment in any
-- part of a country or territory outside Singapore, because of any land or forest fire on any land situated outside Singapore; and
-- (b) ... the smoke from that fire is likely to move in the direction of Singapore", the Director-General may give a notice "to any
-- entity" that in his or her opinion is directly or indirectly involved in conduct causing or likely to cause haze pollution in
-- Singapore. No haze pollution in Singapore is required.
GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Person, `air pollution in Singapore from the fire` IS A BOOLEAN, `air pollution abroad from the fire` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the smoke is likely to move toward Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `the recipient is thought to be involved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a preventive measures notice may be given` IF
        `is an entity` `the recipient`
    AND (`air pollution in Singapore from the fire` OR `air pollution abroad from the fire`)
    AND `the smoke is likely to move toward Singapore`
    AND `the recipient is thought to be involved`

§§ `10, 14, 19 -- other offences and composition`

-- s 10(6): failing to comply with an information notice "without reasonable excuse": a fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment
-- not exceeding one month or both. s 10(7): intentionally altering, suppressing or destroying required documents, or a knowingly or
-- recklessly false statement: $5,000 or 3 months or both. s 14: obstructing, hindering or delaying the Director-General or an
-- authorised officer: (a) $10,000 or 3 months or both; (b) on a second or subsequent conviction, $20,000 or 3 months or both.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `causing or condoning haze pollution`
    `failing to comply with an information notice`
    `destroying or falsifying required information`
    `obstructing an officer, first conviction`
    `obstructing an officer, repeat conviction`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `causing or condoning haze pollution` THEN 2000000
    WHEN `failing to comply with an information notice` THEN 5000
    WHEN `destroying or falsifying required information` THEN 5000
    WHEN `obstructing an officer, first conviction` THEN 10000
    WHEN `obstructing an officer, repeat conviction` THEN 20000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `causing or condoning haze pollution` THEN 0
    WHEN `failing to comply with an information notice` THEN 1
    OTHERWISE 3

-- s 10(6) applies "without reasonable excuse".
GIVEN `was served with an information notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the section 10(6) offence` IF
    `was served with an information notice` AND `failed to comply` AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

-- s 19(1): the Director-General may compound an offence "that is prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum not
-- exceeding the lower of ... (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $5,000." Which
-- offences are prescribed was not retrieved; this is the ceiling only.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition ceiling for` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the maximum fine for` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

§§ `15, 16 -- service and officers`

-- s 15(2)(b): a notice "sent by prepaid registered post ... is deemed to have been duly served ... 2 days after the day the notice
-- or document was posted, whether or not it is returned undelivered." (Days as day numbers.)
GIVEN `the day of posting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deemed day of service by registered post` MEANS
    `the day of posting` PLUS 2

-- s 16(1): where an offence under this Act is committed by a body corporate, unincorporated association or partnership, an officer
-- or partner "purporting to act in such capacity shall be guilty of that offence ... unless the person proves, on a balance of
-- probabilities -- (a) that the offence was committed without the person's consent, connivance or privity; and (b) that the person
-- exercised all such diligence to prevent the commission of the offence as the person ought to have exercised".
GIVEN `the body committed an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `was an officer or partner at the time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved no consent, connivance or privity` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved all due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
        `the body committed an offence under this Act`
    AND `was an officer or partner at the time`
    AND (NOT (`proved no consent, connivance or privity` AND `proved all due diligence`))
